# Charge the pack to its rated voltage, not the charger chip's default.
#
# The BQ24297 powers up with a 4.208 V constant-charge voltage, which never
# fills this 4.34 V pack -- it stops somewhere short of full and the gauge
# correctly never reaches 100%. The charger driver can take the right value
# from a "monitored-battery" phandle, and that is the idiomatic place for it,
# but doing so has an unwanted side effect: bq24190 then also publishes
# charge-full-design on its own battery power-supply, which has no charge
# reading of its own. upower sees a second 27.8 Wh battery stuck at 0%,
# averages it with the real one, and the desktop shows half the true charge.
# upower 1.91 dropped UPOWER_IGNORE, so there is no way to hide it.
#
# Setting the voltage directly avoids handing the charger battery data it
# cannot measure against. Revisit if bq24190 stops advertising a capacity it
# does not know, or if upower learns to weight batteries by measurable energy.
SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", KERNEL=="bq24190-charger", ATTR{constant_charge_voltage}="4340000"
